          ['The harvest window is narrow and unforgiving','The target is 30–35% dry matter, with the kernel milk line between one-half and two-thirds down the kernel. The crop dries down at roughly 0.5–0.6 percentage points of moisture per day, so the window is a matter of days rather than weeks.'],
          ['It is the most energy-dense forage a ruminant system can grow at scale','Well-eared maize silage carries 26–39% starch, total digestible nutrients of 62–74% and metabolisable energy of 10.8–11.5 MJ per kg of dry matter. No other forage a Sahelian producer can grow at field scale combines that energy density with that tonnage per hectare.']
