      s7:{
        n:'07', label:'SECTION 07', name:'Conclusions and the programme',
        lede:'The findings consolidated, their limits stated, and a replicated national programme recommended — from West Africa, a message to the continent.',
        h:'Findings',
        findings:[
          'Every NANOTERN-treated parcel outyielded its paired control, under half the recorded mineral fertilizer and approximately half the irrigation events.',
          'The aggregate gain across three paired hectares was +18.8% by tonnage; the mean of the three parcel gains was +19.1%; the leading pair returned +40%.',
          'Yield per irrigation event and per kilogram of fertilizer product more than doubled in all three pairs — the gain is a multiple, not a margin.',
          'Independent satellite monitoring, contracted before sowing and reported three times in season, recorded no decline in crop development on any treated parcel under the reduced regime.',
          'The combination of granular placement and liquid delivery outperformed either alone, indicating a complementary effect worth isolating in the next cycle.'
        ],
        limitsLabel:'THE LIMITS, STATED',
        limits:[
          'Parcel-level metered irrigation volumes were not captured in the 2026 season; the reduction is established on event frequency and the farm\u2019s own characterisation, not on measured cubic metres.',
          'The field log does not capture any base dressing applied before the trial period, so total season nutrition per parcel should be metered and reported in the next cycle.',
          'The gross margin figure of approximately 30% is preliminary and requires a detailed local input-cost breakdown before general citation.',
          'One site, one season, one crop. Replication across agro-ecological zones is the condition of national inference.'
        ],
        recLabel:'RECOMMENDATIONS',
        recs:[
          ['01','A replicated national programme','Extend the paired-control, satellite-verified protocol across Senegal\u2019s five agro-ecological zones, beginning in the Groundnut Basin on Tassette\u2019s own soils.'],
          ['02','Full instrumentation','Meter irrigation volumes and total season nutrition at parcel level, so the next report states cubic metres and kilograms of nutrient rather than event frequency.'],
          ['03','Isolate the combination effect','Design the next cycle to separate the granular, liquid and combined treatments at replicate scale, and to test rate response.'],
          ['04','Prepare the economics','Complete a local input-cost breakdown so the margin case can be stated with the same confidence as the agronomic one.']
        ],
        africaLabel:'FOR SENEGAL AND FOR AFRICA',
        africa:'What was demonstrated at Tassette is not specific to Senegal. Sandy profiles, a shortened rainy season, imported fertilizer and falling water tables describe the working conditions of much of the continent. A technology that holds water and nutrient where the crop feeds is, in that context, infrastructure — and it can be deployed on existing equipment, in the current season, at farm scale.',
        attLabel:'ATTESTATION',
        att:'This report was prepared by ANT Systems Holding B.V., the Netherlands. The primary field record was kept by the Tassette Farm agronomic team; satellite monitoring was performed and reported independently by Doktar Technologies. Figures are reproduced from that record without adjustment.',
        ref:'NANOTERN Official Field Trial Report · ANT-SN-2026-01 · 31 July 2026'
      },

